{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at `bfd1ea7d641ac73411878d613c3017c1222090ee`, tree `ead96ec2`. The repair removes the gap that the native witness names. Three items below need an owner, and none of them blocks this landing.\n\n**What I checked.** I read the note, the diff of `data.ts`, the probe and the harness, and the callers of `verifiedRoom`, `actsOn` and `loadChange` in `main.ts`. I ran `roster-refresh.scope.test.ts` and `assets.test.ts` once at this head: both pass, and the worktree stays clean. Both `SHA256SUMS` files and the manifest match the request's digests, and the unit's checksums pass. All 19 digests in the note's table name files in the manifest, and all 52 listed files match. My own text scan for link, key, JWT and bearer patterns found nothing in the 193 files. `git diff f51fbf5d bfd1ea7d` names only the note and the manifest, so gate exit 0 and Page workflow 41369009582, success at `f51fbf5d`, carry to this head.\n\n**The cause holds locally.** `room.me = null` before the await left the cached room unverified, and `main.ts:1021` then throws the exact words that `replay/result.json` captured at opening 80. The first local run used Page bytes equal to the deployed source (`page-byte-guard.json`: same) and failed at press 15 with no observer. `causal/before.log` fails on the pending-identity assertion. Both final controls report DISTINGUISHES on their named assertions.\n\n**How far 100 of 100 goes.** The native witness and the two controls carry the cause. The clean count cannot do that alone, because three of the five unfixed runs also opened 100 rows. Those three ran with observers, and the note lists each observer's possible effect on timing. The note calls the count bounded local script evidence and keeps the limit that planner `3b56d034` asked for: this does not assign the earlier hosted stop the same cause.\n\n**Architecture: sound.** One function now owns the roster read for both callers. A `WeakMap` keyed by room suits this, because `ownedRoom` copies a room for each observation, and each copy gets its own entry. So a copy's expiry signal cannot reject another caller's read. Only one read runs per room, so reads cannot publish out of order.\n\n**Security: no new authority.** Keeping the prior identity during a read gives a draw what it already had between reads. `actsOn` and the reviewer choices in `loadChange` still await the read before they use the result, and the test shows that a completed roster removes the act. A caller that joins a pending read can see a roster that started up to one read earlier, and the scope still judges every act. A failed read clears standing, and the failed-read control distinguishes that. The probe records no headers or bodies, strips query strings, and keeps keys under `WITNESS_PRIVATE_DIR`.\n\n**Simplification: one dead line.** `needs-you-browser.mjs:182` adds `const { reasonLines } = await load(\"apps/views/src/attention.ts\");`, and nothing uses `reasonLines`. Main does not hold that line. It costs nothing at runtime beyond the load, and removing it would not justify another gate, so the builder removes it at the next edit of this file.\n\n**Items that need an owner.**\n\n1. **A failed roster read leaves the open Page refused until a reload. This comes from a code read, and no run shows it.** `RoomOpening` clears only a rejected opening, and `opened.clear()` runs only at three sign-in and creation paths. After a failed read, the cached room holds `me: null`, so the next draw throws at `main.ts:1021` before it reaches `actsOn`. The person then sees \"Refused because this key has no verified membership in this room.\" about a membership that may be fine. Main behaves the same way, so this is no regression. The test's \"RECOVERY\" line calls `actsOn` directly, so it shows recovery in the data function and not in a draw. The hosted stop answered 200 on every request, which gives no sign that this path caused it. The planner names an owner, and I recommend a request of its own before the first press work.\n2. **Stream 503s lose their owner at this landing.** The note assigns \"Stream fallback\" to `3b7c6b0b`, and that request closes when this head lands. The unit shows 30 `/stream` 503 diagnostics in the fixed run and a run of 15 within about 7 seconds in the diagnostic run. The polling fallback hid them from the row press. The planner names an owner, or rules that a local Worker's limit explains them.\n3. **The shipped probe still fails on those 503s.** `ROW_PRESS_PROBE=1` checks `repeated.console` against an empty list, so a run with a stream 503 exits 1 after 100 good openings. Three of the three completed runs did so. The clean result came from `verify-fixed.mjs`, which lives only in the evidence unit and counts `/stream` 503s separately. The next person who runs the shipped probe should expect exit 1, and the note does not say so. The builder carries the rule into `needs-you-browser.mjs` when it next edits the file, or says that it will not.\n\nJ5 acceptance stays open under `ff7f7671`, as the note says.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d62862ab28c5e535defdc423fde5eb390f413650","binding":"assigned","head":"bfd1ea7d641ac73411878d613c3017c1222090ee","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6db21f19eae30efd1bd4b58e95216a2ca25f56b2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:510f23bfa0caf8bbffc50af1510917e90b427502\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6db21f19eae30efd1bd4b58e95216a2ca25f56b2","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}